    <item><headword id="d0e190" type="heading" level="h2">(c) Actual dividing and allocating of land, e.g. casting lots</headword></item>
    <item>
      <headword id="d0e195">[crann]</headword>
      <description>a’ dol a chrann, a’ cur a chrann – casting lots. Casting lots in Barrapol, Tiree was used most commonly in the dividing-up of seaweed on the shore amongst the township crofters. Two bodaich would draw aside from the group. One felt his pockets for objects (e.g. a pipe, a knife, a penny, etc.) and the other decided which lot each object represented. Then the first bodach held the objects in the palm of his hand for picking. Never more than ½ doz lots.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="d0e204">[crìochan]</headword>
      <description>boundaries. Crìochan of lots marked out by furrows with ceaba, or by tangles (stamhan).</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="d0e213">a’ togail chrìochan</headword>
      <description>constructing boundaries.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="d0e222">a’ càradh chrìochan</headword>
      <description>mending or maintaining boundaries.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="d0e231">a’ tomhas chrìochan</headword>
      <description>marking boundaries (done by pacing).</description>
    </item>
